<title>NORWAY: Bergesen sells dry bulk ship for $14 mln.</title>
<headline>Bergesen sells dry bulk ship for $14 mln.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norway's largest shipping company Bergesen ASA said on Friday it had sold the 143,000 deadweight-tonne dry bulk vessel, Berge Master, to a Greek buyer for $14 million.</p>
<p>The vessel will change owners in August, Bergesen said in a statement to the Oslo bourse.</p>
<p>Bergesen said it would book a profit of 17 million crowns in the third quarter corresponding to its 65 percent stake in the vessel.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 14</p>
</text>
